  "step_3": "The decision reason evaluates which lottery is more left-skewed (i.e., has more probability weight on favorable outcomes). However, both lotteries have symmetric or neutral skewness: A is deterministic (no skew), B is symmetric around zero (no skew). So the reason cannot clearly prefer one over the other. The individual, in contrast, bases their choice on the certainty of outcome in A and fear of losing 3000€ in B. There is no mention or implication of assessing the shape of the distribution or comparing probabilities of favorable vs. unfavorable outcomes in a skewness-based way. The justification is grounded in risk aversion and loss aversion, not in distributional asymmetry. Therefore, the decision reason was not used. The information considered and the justification do not align with the skewness-based rule.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
}

